## Calculate Tax

Computes the tax on a taxable amount at a Tax Jurisdiction's rate, rounded to the cent. It takes a plain number, so it works for anything taxed (an invoice, an order, a quote) without knowing which.

```ts
import CalculateTaxCommand from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/commerce/commands/calculate-tax-command';

let { taxableAmount, taxAmount, rateApplied } = await new CalculateTaxCommand(
  commandContext,
).execute({ taxableAmount: 1000, jurisdiction });
```

The rate comes from the Tax Jurisdiction record the caller supplies; there is no live lookup against a tax authority. A jurisdiction with no rate is refused rather than taxed at zero, and so is a negative amount.

### Example

California, United States, at 7.25%.

### Non-goals

Writing the result anywhere (the caller decides), tax exemptions, and compound or tiered rates.
